# Jarvis — AI-Powered Voice Assistant

## 1. Project Overview

Jarvis is a Python-based voice-activated virtual assistant designed to interact with users through voice commands. It combines speech recognition, voice responses, automation, and AI-powered conversational capabilities to make everyday computer tasks easier.

The assistant listens for a wake word, activates when the user says "Jarvis," and responds to supported commands. It can provide spoken responses, open websites, play music, and use an AI API to answer general questions.

## 2. Problem Statement

Using a computer often requires users to perform repetitive manual operations, such as opening websites, searching for information, playing music, and switching between applications.

Traditional interfaces require users to interact through a keyboard and mouse. This can be inconvenient when hands-free interaction is preferred.

The problem is to develop a simple, voice-controlled assistant that understands spoken commands, performs supported tasks automatically, and provides responses through speech.

## 3. Proposed Solution

To solve this problem, I developed Jarvis, a voice-activated virtual assistant using Python.

The system captures audio through a microphone, converts speech into text, identifies the user's request, and executes the corresponding action. It uses text-to-speech technology to communicate with the user.

For general conversational questions, the assistant can connect to an AI language model through an API.

The solution combines voice interaction, task automation, and AI-based responses in one application.

## 4. Project Objectives

- Develop a voice-controlled virtual assistant using Python.
- Recognize a wake word to activate the assistant.
